  "text": "Allergies:\ntetracycline / Nitroimidazoles / Penicillins\n\nChief Complaint:\nepigastric pain\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ year old male with a history of\natrial fibrillation reports some chest pressure with exertion\nthat is relieved with rest. He was sent for a stress ___ that\nwas found to be abnormal and was referred for a cardiac\ncatheterization. Catheterization revealed 3 vessel disease\nincluding left main and he is now being referred to cardiac\nsurgery for surgical revascularization.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nThe ___ is a ___ man with worsening symptoms related \nto coronary disease, also has paroxysmal atrial fibrillation, \npresenting for surgery. After usual preoperative workup, on \n___ ___ was taken to the operating room and \nunderwent 1. Coronary artery bypass grafting x3, left internal \nmammary artery graft to left anterior descending,reverse \nsaphenous vein graft to the ___ marginal branch and the \nposterior descending artery.2. Modified left-sided Maze with \nradiofrequency ablation of  the pulmonary veins and left atrial \nappendage ligation with ___. Please see operative note \nfor further surgical details. He tolerated the procedure well \nand wastransferred to the CVICU for invasive monitoring. He \nweaned off of pressor support. Beta-blocker/Statin/ASA and \ndiuresis were initiated. Chest tubes and pacing wires were \ndiscontinued per protocol without incident. Postoperatively his \nrhythm was atrial fibrillation. Anticoagulation was resumed with \nCoumadin. He was placed on Amiodarone s/p MAZE. His INR became \nsupratherapeutic likely because of the Amiodarone potentiating \nthe Coumadin. His Coumadin was held and his INR was allowed to \ndrift down. He transferred to the step down unit for further \nmonitoring. Physical Therapy was consulted for evaluation of \nstrength and mobility. His abdomen was softly distended. KUB \nrevealed dilated loop of bowel. Bowel regimen was increased and \ndiet adjusted to rest bowel. Over the next several days he moved \nhis bowels, passing flatus, LFTs normal, diet advanced and the \npt felt well. On serial KUBs his bowel remains dilated. He was \nplaced on Reglan IV while in house and po for his discharge. His \nINR was still supratherapeutic by the time of discharge despite  \nCoumadin being held for several days to allow it to drift down. \nHe will have his INR drawn the day after discharge by ___. By \nthe time of discharge on pod#7 he was ambulating independently, \nwounds healing, and pain controlled. He was discharged to home \nwith ___ services. All follow up appointments were advised.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nCAD",
